title: $:/nikorion/language/en-GB/ThemeNotice/

Title: ! Everything you edit or create here becomes the theme
Rule: ''In this dev wiki, whatever you create or modify from the web interface is part of the plugin.'' It is written into `src/theme/` and removed from `wiki/tiddlers/`: you build the theme directly in the browser.
Why: The dev server watches what the browser saves. A tiddler the plugin already ships updates its source file (a `.tid`, or a line of `overrides/vanilla.multids`). A new one is created in the plugin: a stylesheet in `styles/`, a new Vanilla setting in `vanilla.multids`, an image in `images/`, anything else (palette, view, settings, notes…) in `overrides/`. Only works while `pnpm dev` runs.
Where: Never taken: drafts, session state, and the tiddlers that were already files of this wiki when the server started (this one, Playground, site title…): their edits stay in the wiki. Check `git status` in the plugin after a session: new files in `styles/` and `overrides/` are what you created.
Manual: ''Creating a file by hand in `wiki/tiddlers/` while `pnpm dev` runs would make the plugin swallow it as theme.'' Create wiki content (a demo, a note) before starting `pnpm dev`, or stop the server while you do it.
